# The built llama-server (scripts/build-llama-server.sh), about 15 MB of
# per-architecture Mach-O. It must never be committed.
#
# The `!` negation that used to be here is gone. It un-ignored exactly the file
# the build replaces, which is the file most likely to be 15 MB, so `git add -A`
# staged the real binary. The path is still required to exist at bundle time
# (tauri.conf.json maps binaries/llama-server), but nothing needs it *tracked*:
# both CI jobs and any local build run build-llama-server.sh first, which
# creates it. `scripts/check-no-built-binaries.sh` is the second line of
# defence, in case a future edit reintroduces a tracking exception.
crates/teletype-desktop/binaries/

